__pycache__/
*.pyc
capture.log
early_vs_sp_*.json

# The app database is ~100 MB and grows daily, which is past GitHub's 100 MB
# per-file HARD limit - pushes were being rejected and the deployed app was
# frozen on an old copy.  It now travels as racing_form.db.gz (~26 MB) and
# app.py unpacks it on cold start.  See scripts/pack_cloud_db.py
racing_form.db
racing_form.db.unpacking
racing_form.db.download

# ...and since 2026-09-24 the gzip is a GitHub RELEASE ASSET, not a committed file:
# a ~29 MB binary every 2 hours was ~350 MB a day of git history, and both the
# laptop pipeline and the cloud Action wrote it, so their branches diverged and each
# could overwrite the other's settlement.  See tools/publish_release_asset.py.
racing_form.db.gz

# secrets must never be committed - add them in Streamlit Cloud's
# App Settings -> Secrets, or keep them in a local file that stays here
.streamlit/secrets.toml
.streamlit/
secrets.toml
bf_token.json
*.log
